      "issue": 1333,
      "state": "closed",
      "url": "https://github.com/den-run-ai/pystachy/issues/1333",
      "body": "## Problem\n\nA base-typed read of an exception field can segfault when a subclass shadows that field with a mutable class attribute. The regression in #1278 exits with SIGSEGV in native JIT and AOT on both alpha.5 (`b2182a4f`) and alpha.6 candidate `6e02b36b`; pinned CPython 3.13.16 completes normally.\n\n## Scope\n\n#1389 merged this isolated correction at `30822255` for RC.1. Normal/stressed JIT/AOT, retained IR comparison, fresh review and all required exact-main gates passed.\n\nQualify the isolated compiler correction [b27908f4](https://github.com/den-run-ai/pystachy/commit/b27908f43e8cd7f6af763d747d89c25b0fb2aad2) and its three regression programs separately from #1278's broader Lean work. It supplies shared assignment flags and subclass-selected class-attribute fallbacks. The current evidence establishes a pre-existing accepted-program crash; new class-value handlers bind a generic exception and do not directly introduce this projection. Refs #1186. Investigation assisted by ChatGPT.\n\n## Done when\n\nBefore RC.1, the isolated fix matches pinned CPython for base methods, typed parameters, handlers, deep inheritance, changed defaults, instance writes, missing fields and `hasattr`; normal and stressed JIT/AOT, all affected IR differences, current-head review and required CI pass on merged main."
    },
    {
      "issue": 1358,
      "state": "closed",
      "url": "https://github.com/den-run-ai/pystachy/issues/1358",
      "body": "## Problem\n\nA builtin call whose union argument's members all give `None` is joined with an LLVM `phi void`. On main `1ab0b93` (hosted compiler), CPython prints `slept 0.001` for:\n\n```python\nimport time\n\nLIMIT = 24 * 3600\n\n\ndef wait(t: float) -> None:\n    timeout = t\n    if timeout > LIMIT:\n        timeout = LIMIT  # int | float\n    time.sleep(timeout)\n    print(\"slept\", timeout)\n\n\nwait(0.001)\n```\n\nPystachy calls `pys_sleep` and `pys_sleep_int` per member, then emits `%t38 = phi void [null, %L28], [null, %L35]`, which LLVM's `opt` rejects (\"void type only allowed for function results\"). `PYSTACHY_IRCHECK=1` accepts the IR. `abs()`, `math.sqrt()` and `float()` of the same local compile. #1279's `lib/asyncio` works around it with [`float(MAXIMUM_SELECT_TIMEOUT)`](https://github.com/den-run-ai/pystachy/blob/916ef7b75da6f5d5e3853c877fdc1a0fd014920d/lib/asyncio/base_events.py#L339).\n\n## Scope\n\n#1363 merged through #1389 at `30822255` for RC.1. Its regression and all required exact-main gates passed.\n\n[`gen_usplit`](https://github.com/den-run-ai/pystachy/blob/1ab0b934183e17bca517372181151f725f5e7ba5/src/pystachy_compiler/union_arithmetic.py#L80-L116) builds the phi without the `None` result that other joins return early. The IR check could also reject `phi void`. Found while porting `asyncio` with Claude Code (AI) assistance. Refs #1279.\n\n## Done when\n\nThe program above matches CPython in the JIT and AOT, a regression lives in `tests/programs/`, and the `asyncio` workaround can be dropped."
    },
    {
      "issue": 1300,
      "state": "closed",
      "url": "https://github.com/den-run-ai/pystachy/issues/1300",
      "body": "## Problem\n\nThe `float` pyperformance port runs 37% slower in AOT since #1268: 32.92 ms at its first parent `0ec827ac`, 43.62 ms at its merge `b40ee875` and 45.11 ms on main `8434a911` (CPython: 508.7 ms). Medians of 15 interleaved runs pinned to one CPU of an idle host.\n\n## Scope\n\n#1336 merged through #1389 as `30822255`. The historical median recovery threshold and all required exact-main gates passed.\n\nInstructions rose only 1.4%; page faults and peak RSS are unchanged. listguard versions `for i in range(n): points[i] = Point(i)` into checked and unchecked loops, so `Point.__init__` gets a second call site and LLVM stops inlining it. With the compiler before #1268, one never-executed extra `Point(0)` call alone gives the same out-of-line constructor and 34.06 to 44.76 ms. Any small callee in a versioned loop is exposed; versioning after inlining, or keeping such callees inlined, would avoid it. [Evidence](https://github.com/den-run-ai/pystachy/blob/4ad35048/research/speed-vs-surface-2026-11-12/followup/README.md#regressions-reproduced-on-main)\n\n## Done when\n\n`float` AOT is within 5% of `0ec827ac` in the same pinned interleaved comparison, with listguard's checks and proofs kept. A deterministic IR or call-count check fails when a versioned loop leaves such a constructor out of line. Prepared with Claude Code assistance."
    }
